still recognisable for the most part. They're much more evocative and playable now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! Improved, evocative, playable, and recognizable were all among our goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13387-jonsan","name":"jonsan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T17:56:49-07:00","id":1090061,"title":"","content":"Which one got the shapeshifter cantrip?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T18:10:16-07:00","id":1090070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089093-what-did-they-do-with-primal?p=1090061#post1090061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which one got the shapeshifter cantrip?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shapeshifting became its own Art called Metamorphosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13387-jonsan","name":"jonsan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T01:14:04-07:00","id":1090170,"title":"","content":"Metamorphoss existed before. Though, it was reworked too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T01:16:38-07:00","id":1090171,"title":"","content":"You can still talk to animals with Primal 1 right, or was it shifted to only elements?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T01:56:22-07:00","id":1090181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089093-what-did-they-do-with-primal?p=1090171#post1090171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can still talk to animals with Primal 1 right, or was it shifted to only elements?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any animal, plant or object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T03:10:53-07:00","id":1090203,"title":"","content":"If you have Primal 3, you won't notice a big difference in your powers.<br /> <br /> Primal 4 can actually be used to heal bashing or lethal, but it's become fun. If you imbue someone with wood then they regenerate 1 lethal every 5 minutes and are quite literally rooted to the spot.<br /> <br /> Primal 5 I like. My crossover game has been converting to the -20 series as it is released and my changeling just started planting a trees in his garden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T12:12:45-07:00","id":1093370,"title":"","content":"New Primal is definitely more focused. That is the thing that has most come out of this for many of the Arts; they are more focused. Legerdemain is more tricksy, Chicanery is... also more tricksy, but in a different way. Primal is more elemental, Metamorphosis more transformative, Pyretics less literal, Soothsay less redundant (I love seeing Willow-the-Wisp there!). Veiled Eyes and Wind Walker are far less roll-and-Glamour-intensive, Ensnare is no longer broken (I had to make rules to stop people from turning marbles into deadly railguns). Skycraft does feel a bit lost in places, but I can get behind the four seasonal Arts; I notice how they absorbed several old Arts or Cantrips, particularly Kryos, Aphrodesia, and Heather Balm. I AM curious if the Denizens and Thallain are still going to get any special Arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}